.TH LISTEN 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
listen \- mark a socket as accepting connections
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B int listen(int descriptor, int backlog);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Marks a socket as passive; backlog requests the maximum queue length.
Linux may cap the backlog.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR accept (3crunch),
.BR listen (2)
